          "**Secretory diarrhoea (cholera, ETEC)**: cholera toxin ADP-ribosylates the Gs protein, locking **adenylate cyclase on**; high **cAMP** opens the **CFTR chloride channel** in crypt cells and blocks NaCl absorption in villous cells, so isotonic fluid pours out - stool volume can reach **100-200 mL/kg/day** (rice-water stools). [Nelson 22e]",
